1
00:00:48,850 --> 00:00:53,030
[The Old Story of Yu Hong]

2
00:00:53,400 --> 00:00:55,670
[Episode 28]

3
00:01:20,530 --> 00:01:21,289
Hao Jie.

4
00:01:22,430 --> 00:01:23,350
I'm back.

5
00:02:17,530 --> 00:02:18,370
Liu Yang,

6
00:02:19,010 --> 00:02:20,670
may this letter find you well.

7
00:02:22,020 --> 00:02:24,510
By the time you read this,

8
00:02:24,640 --> 00:02:26,610
I will have boarded a train

9
00:02:27,300 --> 00:02:28,540
that passes through

10
00:02:28,740 --> 00:02:31,750
the stations whose names
we've recited countless times,

11
00:02:31,750 --> 00:02:33,280
and be heading to the south.

12
00:02:36,130 --> 00:02:37,470
Before departure,

13
00:02:37,650 --> 00:02:39,410
I met with Chen Hong.

14
00:02:40,220 --> 00:02:42,060
Sorry for acting without your permission.

15
00:02:42,060 --> 00:02:44,740
Please forgive me for any pertinence.

16
00:02:46,090 --> 00:02:48,650
She agreed to give me 300 thousand yuan

17
00:02:48,700 --> 00:02:51,160
so I can seek medical treatment
in the south.

18
00:02:51,920 --> 00:02:52,740
In return,

19
00:02:53,390 --> 00:02:56,120
I voluntarily withdraw
from this relationship.

20
00:03:00,270 --> 00:03:02,460
Lately, I often ask myself,

21
00:03:03,460 --> 00:03:05,130
since we first reunited

22
00:03:05,240 --> 00:03:06,700
and got together,

23
00:03:07,500 --> 00:03:08,060
if I have

24
00:03:08,060 --> 00:03:10,560
ever truly loved you.

25
00:03:11,560 --> 00:03:13,830
Every time this thought arises,

26
00:03:13,930 --> 00:03:16,190
I'd feel a deep sense of guilt toward you.

27
00:03:17,560 --> 00:03:19,260
I wish for nothing

28
00:03:19,579 --> 00:03:21,079
but to survive.

29
00:03:24,240 --> 00:03:25,540
To me,

30
00:03:25,790 --> 00:03:27,870
you were just the last lifeline I grasped

31
00:03:27,870 --> 00:03:30,329
when I sank into absolute despair.

32
00:03:32,030 --> 00:03:33,250
Never did I expect you

33
00:03:33,270 --> 00:03:35,300
to sacrifice so much for me.

34
00:03:36,090 --> 00:03:37,030
I am so moved,

35
00:03:37,730 --> 00:03:39,730
but I have nothing to repay you with.

36
00:03:41,620 --> 00:03:43,860
As time went by,

37
00:03:44,020 --> 00:03:45,520
I gradually discovered

38
00:03:45,710 --> 00:03:46,970
that many new feelings

39
00:03:46,970 --> 00:03:48,800
were taking root in my heart—

40
00:03:50,340 --> 00:03:51,370
expectation,

41
00:03:52,090 --> 00:03:53,090
possessiveness,

42
00:03:54,430 --> 00:03:55,590
resentment.

43
00:03:57,360 --> 00:04:00,370
Perhaps this is what people call love.

44
00:04:02,190 --> 00:04:03,590
But even so, what can I do?

45
00:04:04,300 --> 00:04:05,680
Other than continuing to be

46
00:04:05,680 --> 00:04:07,650
a heavy burden to you,

47
00:04:08,240 --> 00:04:10,540
I'm unable to give you a warm embrace

48
00:04:10,650 --> 00:04:14,150
and a cozy life that other women can.

49
00:04:15,790 --> 00:04:17,560
Just trying to survive

50
00:04:18,100 --> 00:04:20,899
has drained all my strength.

51
00:04:23,550 --> 00:04:26,010
Thank you for everything
you've done for me.

52
00:04:26,690 --> 00:04:29,570
Also, please express my gratitude
to Chen Hong.

53
00:04:30,720 --> 00:04:32,380
I sincerely hope the two of you

54
00:04:32,630 --> 00:04:33,860
lead a happy life

55
00:04:34,480 --> 00:04:36,610
and gain success in everything you do.

56
00:04:41,330 --> 00:04:41,930
[Junlan Grand Hotel] [Friendly Reminder]

57
00:04:41,960 --> 00:04:46,350
[Previously]

58
00:04:46,370 --> 00:04:49,600
[Junlan Grand Hotel] [Friendly Reminder]

59
00:04:50,430 --> 00:04:51,580
Coming!

60
00:05:13,040 --> 00:05:13,880
Have a seat.

61
00:05:48,620 --> 00:05:51,220
After starting dialysis,
I stopped producing urine.

62
00:05:51,220 --> 00:05:52,550
My kidneys have shrunk,

63
00:05:52,930 --> 00:05:54,790
so I dare not drink too much water.

64
00:06:03,940 --> 00:06:05,140
How far along are you?

65
00:06:07,620 --> 00:06:08,950
Less than three months.

66
00:06:15,840 --> 00:06:17,570
Just about as long as I guessed.

67
00:06:19,770 --> 00:06:21,030
Because of my illness,

68
00:06:22,300 --> 00:06:24,700
Yang has been subjected to much suffering.

69
00:06:26,570 --> 00:06:28,570
It's actually fine the way it is now.

70
00:06:43,650 --> 00:06:45,180
In fact, I'm jealous of you.

71
00:06:48,040 --> 00:06:49,770
Jealous of me being severely ill?

72
00:06:49,770 --> 00:06:50,300
Yes.

73
00:06:51,010 --> 00:06:53,740
I'm jealous that you have everything
but health,

74
00:06:54,000 --> 00:06:55,200
like the love of a man.

75
00:06:59,010 --> 00:07:00,620
Now, I only want to survive.

76
00:07:08,310 --> 00:07:09,440
I'm in need of money.

77
00:07:10,010 --> 00:07:11,980
I plan to go to Shanghai,
wait in line for a kidney donor,

78
00:07:11,980 --> 00:07:13,840
and receive a kidney transplant.

79
00:07:14,000 --> 00:07:15,220
If you agree to help,

80
00:07:16,060 --> 00:07:17,720
I'll leave Yang immediately.

81
00:07:34,120 --> 00:07:35,310
How much do you need?

82
00:07:59,430 --> 00:08:01,160
When it comes to staying alive,

83
00:08:03,440 --> 00:08:05,000
nothing is off-limits.

84
00:08:23,150 --> 00:08:26,830
[Golden Imperial Dance Hall]

85
00:08:28,240 --> 00:08:28,510
You go first.

86
00:08:28,510 --> 00:08:29,240
The usual place.

87
00:08:29,240 --> 00:08:30,130
Absolutely.

88
00:08:31,220 --> 00:08:33,000
What are you guys talking about?

89
00:08:33,000 --> 00:08:33,580
You can do that too?

90
00:08:33,580 --> 00:08:34,580
I saw her palm that day. It was different.

91
00:08:34,580 --> 00:08:35,620
Come on, give me your hand.

92
00:08:35,620 --> 00:08:36,049
Look.

93
00:08:36,049 --> 00:08:37,270
What do you see in my palm?

94
00:08:37,270 --> 00:08:37,789
Big Fella.

95
00:08:37,789 --> 00:08:38,390
Big Fella!

96
00:08:38,460 --> 00:08:40,860
-Quite messy.
-You sure you can read palms?

97
00:08:41,620 --> 00:08:42,419
Dong, come...

98
00:08:42,980 --> 00:08:43,740
Yan'er, it's you!

99
00:08:43,740 --> 00:08:44,740
When did you get back?

100
00:08:44,740 --> 00:08:45,840
Several days ago.

101
00:08:46,050 --> 00:08:46,940
Where is Dong?

102
00:08:46,940 --> 00:08:47,540
No idea.

103
00:08:47,960 --> 00:08:49,520
Dong didn't show up today.

104
00:08:49,550 --> 00:08:50,380
He didn't?

105
00:08:50,720 --> 00:08:52,390
We haven't seen Dong for days.

106
00:08:52,390 --> 00:08:53,170
Your palm lines are messy.

107
00:08:53,170 --> 00:08:54,500
I read hers before.

108
00:08:54,500 --> 00:08:55,430
Look at mine now.

109
00:08:55,670 --> 00:08:56,550
These lines...

110
00:08:59,150 --> 00:09:01,830
Could something have happened to Dong?

111
00:09:03,650 --> 00:09:04,220
What?

112
00:09:07,050 --> 00:09:08,450
The third incense stick.

113
00:09:13,050 --> 00:09:13,860
No more chatter!

114
00:09:13,860 --> 00:09:14,700
Let's go look for him!

115
00:09:14,700 --> 00:09:15,230
Let's go.

116
00:09:18,340 --> 00:09:18,940
Is he in there?

117
00:09:18,940 --> 00:09:19,830
No.

118
00:09:20,510 --> 00:09:21,100
Did you search carefully?

119
00:09:21,100 --> 00:09:21,700
Yes, I did.

120
00:09:21,700 --> 00:09:22,270
Did you find him?

121
00:09:22,270 --> 00:09:23,130
-No.
-Not a trace.

122
00:09:23,130 --> 00:09:23,790
Dong!

123
00:09:23,790 --> 00:09:24,500
Dong.

124
00:09:24,620 --> 00:09:25,620
Dong.

125
00:09:26,170 --> 00:09:26,840
Dong!

126
00:09:26,840 --> 00:09:27,770
Did you find him?

127
00:09:28,200 --> 00:09:29,820
-No. What about you?
-You guys found him or not?

128
00:09:29,820 --> 00:09:30,400
No.

129
00:09:30,510 --> 00:09:32,440
Are you stupid or what?
Could Dong be in here?

130
00:09:32,440 --> 00:09:33,600
It's possible.

131
00:09:35,130 --> 00:09:35,550
Dong!

132
00:09:35,550 --> 00:09:36,130
Dong!

133
00:09:36,460 --> 00:09:37,170
Is he there?

134
00:09:37,460 --> 00:09:38,010
No.

135
00:09:38,010 --> 00:09:39,100
Let's move then!

136
00:09:39,630 --> 00:09:41,350
[Welcome]

137
00:09:40,510 --> 00:09:41,440
Go check the car!

138
00:09:42,700 --> 00:09:43,270
Dong.

139
00:09:43,340 --> 00:09:43,770
Dong.

140
00:09:43,770 --> 00:09:44,170
Dong.

141
00:09:44,170 --> 00:09:45,050
Come out, Dong.

142
00:09:45,050 --> 00:09:45,940
Where are you hiding, Dong?

143
00:09:45,940 --> 00:09:46,530
Any findings in the back?

144
00:09:46,530 --> 00:09:47,210
Dong!

145
00:09:47,270 --> 00:09:47,840
Dong.

146
00:09:47,840 --> 00:09:48,610
Dong.

147
00:09:49,840 --> 00:09:50,840
Let's check over there!

148
00:09:50,840 --> 00:09:51,390
Inquire properly!

149
00:09:51,390 --> 00:09:52,390
Ask each of them!

150
00:09:52,890 --> 00:09:53,940
Sir, have you seen this man?

151
00:09:53,940 --> 00:09:55,000
Stop eating. Take a look at this.

152
00:09:55,000 --> 00:09:56,080
Have you seen this man?

153
00:09:56,080 --> 00:09:57,290
Eyes on the photo, not me!

154
00:09:57,290 --> 00:09:58,000
Have you seen this man?

155
00:09:58,000 --> 00:09:58,840
Have you seen this person?

156
00:09:58,840 --> 00:09:59,340
Have you seen this man?

157
00:09:59,340 --> 00:09:59,960
He's named Dong.

158
00:09:59,960 --> 00:10:00,630
Is it good?

159
00:10:00,630 --> 00:10:00,910
Good.

160
00:10:00,910 --> 00:10:02,510
Talking to you is such a pain.

161
00:10:02,890 --> 00:10:03,860
Never seen him, huh?

162
00:10:03,860 --> 00:10:05,240
Why is it so hard to talk to you?

163
00:10:05,240 --> 00:10:06,130
I'm taking all these.

164
00:10:06,130 --> 00:10:06,860
How did it go?

165
00:10:07,510 --> 00:10:09,510
Go over there and inquire properly.

166
00:10:09,580 --> 00:10:10,680
Ask carefully.

167
00:10:11,240 --> 00:10:12,970
These bananas are really good.

168
00:10:13,120 --> 00:10:14,130
Fully ripe.

169
00:10:15,290 --> 00:10:16,250
So sweet.

170
00:10:17,960 --> 00:10:18,750
Auntie,

171
00:10:19,980 --> 00:10:21,310
for the past half month,

172
00:10:21,600 --> 00:10:23,200
I've kept many words inside.

173
00:10:23,510 --> 00:10:24,510
I'm done with it.,

174
00:10:25,510 --> 00:10:27,570
Come on, taste this. See if it's soft.

175
00:10:27,840 --> 00:10:29,560
It's fully ripe. Take a bite.

176
00:10:32,320 --> 00:10:33,270
Not bad, huh?

177
00:10:39,290 --> 00:10:41,010
Our family failed Jie.

178
00:10:46,600 --> 00:10:48,330
Liu Yang is my younger brother.

179
00:10:48,820 --> 00:10:49,750
If I scold him

180
00:10:49,750 --> 00:10:51,190
for being poorly raised,

181
00:10:51,320 --> 00:10:53,630
wouldn't that be a reprimand
to myself too?

182
00:10:53,630 --> 00:10:55,760
He wasn't like this when he was little.

183
00:10:55,890 --> 00:10:57,790
He would offer his little bowl of food

184
00:10:57,790 --> 00:10:59,630
when he saw the puppy next door

185
00:10:59,630 --> 00:11:00,230
starving.

186
00:11:00,700 --> 00:11:02,700
How did he grow into what he is now?

187
00:11:06,010 --> 00:11:08,210
Here we are, just the two of us chatting.

188
00:11:09,050 --> 00:11:09,910
See, people all

189
00:11:10,770 --> 00:11:12,300
have desires and emotions.

190
00:11:15,200 --> 00:11:16,400
This is human nature.

191
00:11:17,410 --> 00:11:19,540
Everyone has a good side and a bad side.

192
00:11:21,000 --> 00:11:23,600
I'm not trying to defend my brother.

193
00:11:25,010 --> 00:11:27,340
But the problem lies in that woman. She...

194
00:11:27,700 --> 00:11:28,560
she already...

195
00:11:30,010 --> 00:11:30,670
Right, huh?

196
00:11:30,720 --> 00:11:32,380
I-It is a human life after all.

197
00:11:32,500 --> 00:11:34,430
I'm really at my wits' end. Really.

198
00:11:37,050 --> 00:11:37,870
Auntie,

199
00:11:40,050 --> 00:11:41,710
do you think the blame's on me?

200
00:11:51,130 --> 00:11:52,460
There is a family matter

201
00:11:53,580 --> 00:11:55,180
that I've never told anyone.

202
00:11:56,320 --> 00:11:57,720
When Liu Yang was little,

203
00:12:01,250 --> 00:12:02,370
I once saw our dad

204
00:12:02,370 --> 00:12:04,300
stealing rice and flour from home.

205
00:12:04,530 --> 00:12:05,500
Our mom caught him

206
00:12:05,500 --> 00:12:06,700
and lashed out at him.

207
00:12:07,130 --> 00:12:08,860
He said it was for his mistress.

208
00:12:10,080 --> 00:12:11,550
Auntie, do you think
this is what people call

209
00:12:11,550 --> 00:12:12,950
"like father, like son"?

210
00:12:14,120 --> 00:12:15,460
Maybe this is all my fault.

211
00:12:15,460 --> 00:12:16,480
I knew that...

212
00:12:16,630 --> 00:12:18,250
Wh-Where is my money?

213
00:12:18,250 --> 00:12:19,370
What money?

214
00:12:19,750 --> 00:12:20,650
What do you mean?

215
00:12:20,650 --> 00:12:21,620
Why is my money gone?

216
00:12:21,620 --> 00:12:23,480
-I need to buy food and cook for my kids.
-We are...

217
00:12:23,480 --> 00:12:25,460
-We are chatting.
-No. Where's my money?

218
00:12:25,460 --> 00:12:26,480
Look, it's all gone.

219
00:12:26,480 --> 00:12:28,700
Auntie, are you having an episode?

220
00:12:28,700 --> 00:12:30,320
-Where’s my money?
-You said you need... Calm down.

221
00:12:30,320 --> 00:12:30,790
Don't panic.

222
00:12:30,790 --> 00:12:31,960
Look, well...

223
00:12:32,410 --> 00:12:33,010
Look.

224
00:12:33,340 --> 00:12:34,620
I-Is this your money?

225
00:12:34,620 --> 00:12:36,140
Is this yours? Look.

226
00:12:37,080 --> 00:12:38,210
It's back, isn't it?

227
00:12:38,360 --> 00:12:39,240
Right?

228
00:12:39,240 --> 00:12:40,000
Just calm down.

229
00:12:40,000 --> 00:12:41,330
Sit down and let's chat.

230
00:12:41,620 --> 00:12:42,410
Finish the banana.

231
00:12:42,410 --> 00:12:43,790
Where's the other fifty?

232
00:12:43,790 --> 00:12:45,120
What do you mean by that?

233
00:12:45,120 --> 00:12:47,050
There's another fifty-yuan bill.

234
00:12:47,220 --> 00:12:48,510
How is there another one?

235
00:12:48,510 --> 00:12:49,820
-I just gave you a fifty.
-I'm serious.

236
00:12:49,820 --> 00:12:51,010
There should be another fifty.

237
00:12:51,010 --> 00:12:51,650
Don't be like this.

238
00:12:51,650 --> 00:12:52,770
How can you try to swindle me?

239
00:12:52,770 --> 00:12:53,510
I-Isn't this it?

240
00:12:53,510 --> 00:12:54,200
What the heck?

241
00:12:54,200 --> 00:12:56,510
It's not. I only have some change
on me now.

242
00:12:56,510 --> 00:12:58,460
-How could you try to swindle...
-I need it to buy food for my kids.

243
00:12:58,460 --> 00:13:00,050
How could you try to swindle me?

244
00:13:00,050 --> 00:13:01,320
Why did I even come

245
00:13:01,320 --> 00:13:02,340
all the way here?

246
00:13:02,340 --> 00:13:05,120
All the debts that little brat owes
are mine to pay now.

247
00:13:05,120 --> 00:13:06,720
Am I fated to be this unlucky?

248
00:13:11,130 --> 00:13:11,820
You... I...

249
00:13:12,470 --> 00:13:14,400
Now I can't even pay the bus fare...

250
00:13:15,420 --> 00:13:16,260
This is it.

251
00:13:16,870 --> 00:13:18,000
Oh, look at that.

252
00:13:19,820 --> 00:13:21,650
Alright then. Auntie,

253
00:13:22,320 --> 00:13:24,080
eat some more.

254
00:13:26,500 --> 00:13:27,250
This is not enough!

255
00:13:27,250 --> 00:13:27,960
Look!

256
00:13:28,460 --> 00:13:30,460
That's all I got. Knit your sweater.

257
00:13:30,620 --> 00:13:32,000
Take care!

258
00:13:34,220 --> 00:13:35,220
Now this is right.

259
00:13:39,500 --> 00:13:41,360
Where's that money from earlier?

260
00:13:41,700 --> 00:13:42,740
Anyone here?

261
00:13:43,620 --> 00:13:46,220
I've told you many times.
I just didn't see him.

262
00:13:48,100 --> 00:13:48,910
It's you.

263
00:13:51,000 --> 00:13:52,260
Looking for your boss?

264
00:13:54,060 --> 00:13:55,790
I'm here to have my hair washed.

265
00:14:00,130 --> 00:14:03,390
A good number of people come here
looking for him every day.

266
00:14:03,940 --> 00:14:05,960
My door handle's almost broken from that.

267
00:14:05,960 --> 00:14:08,030
The police station is right next door.

268
00:14:08,030 --> 00:14:09,890
Why don't they go seek help there?

269
00:14:12,480 --> 00:14:15,280
Won't that be like a chicken
entering a wolf's den?

270
00:14:15,370 --> 00:14:17,430
The police are also looking for Dong.

271
00:14:17,750 --> 00:14:18,740
Why did Dong

272
00:14:19,290 --> 00:14:20,820
just vanish into thin air?

273
00:14:21,440 --> 00:14:23,040
Did he commit a crime or what?

274
00:14:25,700 --> 00:14:27,510
I'm just an errand boy.

275
00:14:28,000 --> 00:14:29,400
How am I supposed to know?

276
00:14:33,670 --> 00:14:34,860
Haven't you thought

277
00:14:35,370 --> 00:14:36,840
about asking Ms. Wan?

278
00:14:39,740 --> 00:14:43,870
♪ In the first watch,
the crescent moon rises ♪

279
00:14:43,870 --> 00:14:47,670
♪ The spirit drum booms,
resounding by the heavenly gate ♪

280
00:14:47,670 --> 00:14:51,950
♪ Feet treading the Seven Star Step,
hands holding a peach wood basin ♪

281
00:14:51,970 --> 00:14:55,840
♪ Stay not in the wild,
where frost bites deep ♪

282
00:15:03,010 --> 00:15:06,910
♪ In the second watch, dark clouds roll ♪

283
00:15:06,910 --> 00:15:10,740
♪ The spirit bells chime,
calling the three souls home ♪

284
00:15:10,740 --> 00:15:14,200
♪ In the third watch,
clappers shake heaven and earth ♪

285
00:15:14,200 --> 00:15:18,100
♪ All you brothers,
thank the gods for their grace ♪

286
00:15:46,870 --> 00:15:47,870
Ms. Wan,

287
00:15:49,080 --> 00:15:51,820
was Dong taken by the Yellow Immortal?

288
00:15:52,210 --> 00:15:53,870
Don't you talk nonsense here.

289
00:15:54,620 --> 00:15:56,000
The Yellow Immortal

290
00:15:56,120 --> 00:15:57,500
said that Dong

291
00:15:57,500 --> 00:15:59,050
isn't in Yuhong at all.

292
00:15:59,050 --> 00:16:00,440
Then where is he now?

293
00:16:03,340 --> 00:16:06,510
Well... I did a quick divination.

294
00:16:07,250 --> 00:16:08,820
You should head south and look for him!

295
00:16:08,820 --> 00:16:09,980
Got it.

296
00:16:09,980 --> 00:16:11,790
Thank you, Ms. Wan!

297
00:16:16,820 --> 00:16:18,040
Quick, guys!

298
00:16:18,720 --> 00:16:20,240
What are you doing here?

299
00:16:20,240 --> 00:16:21,840
You're making so much noise.

300
00:16:22,700 --> 00:16:23,430
Officer Liu.

301
00:16:31,110 --> 00:16:32,960
Do you think I can't see you

302
00:16:32,960 --> 00:16:33,720
or what?

303
00:16:33,720 --> 00:16:34,880
Am I blind to you?

304
00:16:34,980 --> 00:16:35,600
Juan.

305
00:16:37,790 --> 00:16:38,750
I heard

306
00:16:39,250 --> 00:16:41,510
Liang Zhendong went missing. Is it true?

307
00:16:42,870 --> 00:16:43,870
No, it's not true.

308
00:16:44,130 --> 00:16:45,330
Dong is in seclusion.

309
00:16:45,510 --> 00:16:46,970
Then why did you come here?

310
00:16:48,240 --> 00:16:50,550
Just to ask Ms. Wan about him and have her

311
00:16:50,550 --> 00:16:51,750
pass a message to him.

312
00:16:52,870 --> 00:16:55,080
Can't you call him?

313
00:16:55,200 --> 00:16:56,390
Is Wan Xiuhua more reliable

314
00:16:56,390 --> 00:16:57,130
than China Mobile now?

315
00:16:57,130 --> 00:16:59,130
Dong just has great trust in Ms. Wan.

316
00:17:07,380 --> 00:17:08,780
How is your sister doing?

317
00:17:11,400 --> 00:17:13,550
She called and said
she had arrived in Shanghai.

318
00:17:13,550 --> 00:17:14,810
She told me not to go find her.

319
00:17:14,810 --> 00:17:16,270
And you won't just because she said so?

320
00:17:16,270 --> 00:17:18,069
How could you be this negligent?

321
00:17:18,680 --> 00:17:19,880
She's a girl.

322
00:17:19,880 --> 00:17:21,680
If she trips or falls on the road,

323
00:17:21,790 --> 00:17:23,520
no one will be there to help her.

324
00:17:23,660 --> 00:17:25,190
Are you really not worried?

325
00:17:25,770 --> 00:17:26,569
Listen, Juan.

326
00:17:26,960 --> 00:17:28,359
You know how my sister is.

327
00:17:29,510 --> 00:17:31,570
She has never considered Tiecheng her home
growing up.

328
00:17:31,570 --> 00:17:34,430
And she always talked about
going back to Shanghai.

329
00:17:35,010 --> 00:17:36,610
This time, she left quietly.

330
00:17:37,250 --> 00:17:40,250
I bet she was done being
a burden to my brother-in-law.

331
00:17:40,400 --> 00:17:42,730
You still call Yang your brother-in-law?

332
00:17:43,140 --> 00:17:43,830
Well...

333
00:17:45,070 --> 00:17:47,800
My sister was the one
who insisted on the divorce.

334
00:17:50,550 --> 00:17:52,480
It was Yang who failed your sister.

335
00:17:54,750 --> 00:17:55,960
Don't say that, Juan.

336
00:17:58,250 --> 00:17:59,420
I don't blame him,

337
00:18:00,590 --> 00:18:02,990
and my sister won't let me
blame him either.

338
00:18:07,010 --> 00:18:08,270
Well, if...

339
00:18:09,660 --> 00:18:10,860
you ever see Liu Yang,

340
00:18:11,740 --> 00:18:12,940
tell him

341
00:18:12,940 --> 00:18:14,290
to come home for dinner.

342
00:18:15,090 --> 00:18:16,030
May I come too?

343
00:18:16,530 --> 00:18:17,790
Isn't that obvious?

344
00:18:17,790 --> 00:18:19,650
Do I have to specially invite you?

345
00:18:19,960 --> 00:18:21,160
Cut the crap already.

346
00:18:22,270 --> 00:18:24,030
I'm going to work then, Juan.

347
00:18:24,660 --> 00:18:25,350
I'm leaving.

348
00:18:25,350 --> 00:18:25,920
Go ahead.

349
00:18:25,920 --> 00:18:27,380
Just be careful out there.

350
00:18:27,380 --> 00:18:28,590
Mind your behavior.

351
00:18:28,590 --> 00:18:29,250
You hear me?

352
00:18:30,090 --> 00:18:30,790
Be steady.

353
00:18:30,790 --> 00:18:31,520
Sure, got it.

354
00:18:43,640 --> 00:18:46,610
Hao Jie has arrived in Shanghai
and is in hospital now.

355
00:18:46,610 --> 00:18:48,870
The doctors there are highly competent.

356
00:18:49,070 --> 00:18:50,030
So don't worry.

357
00:18:50,030 --> 00:18:51,630
She'll definitely be cured.

358
00:18:53,180 --> 00:18:53,910
Here you are.

359
00:18:54,550 --> 00:18:55,350
Eat the apple.

360
00:18:55,740 --> 00:18:56,510
Weiguo.
